WEBVTT

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.120
<i>Your lunch got all wet?</i>

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.860
Yeah.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.810
<i>You finally had a date, and those cards 
made everything go crazy again.</i>

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.080
<i>You guys really do have it rough, huh?</i>

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.410
<i>So that's why you're taking another 
shot at making rolled omelets?</i>

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.190
Yeah, but I'm not in any hurry.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.970
I'll cook them later.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.670
<i>You can cook eggs and 
still talk on the phone.</i>

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.360
<i>I mean, you're in middle school now!</i>

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.210
<i>How will you get by if you 
can't multitask some?</i>

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.900
<i>But you don't know why these weird things 
keep appearing and turning into cards?</i>

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:06.940
No...

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:15.730
<b>Thick, Rolled Omelets Made Easy</b>

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.650
<i>But you weren't hurt?</i>

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.390
Syaoran-kun and Tomoyo-chan are both fine.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.910
<i>I was asking about you.</i>

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.070
Oh... No problem! I'm great!

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:17.800
<i>Good. But don't lower your guard.</i>

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.560
<i>If you got hurt, it'd make everyone cry!</i>

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.440
Yeah.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.960
<i>Well, I guess I might cry a little, too.</i>

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.660
<b>Meiling-chan</b>

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.100
<i>Just a teeny, tiny bit!</i>

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.660
<b>
End Call</b>

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.660
Meiling-chan...

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.790
<i>Anyway, I'll call again later. 
Sorry to interrupt your cooking.</i>

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.300
It's okay. Thanks for calling.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.200
Later.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.170
<i>I hope the rolled omelets turn out good.</i>

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.180
<b>Meiling-chan</b>

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.180
<b>I hope the rolled omelets turn out good. 

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.970
All right, back to work!

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:53.980
<b>Sakura and the Sleep Labyrinth</b>

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.800
It's done!

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.280
Hello, this is Sakura.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.860
<i>It's Fujitaka. Do you have a second?</i>

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.000
Sure. I just finished my rolled omelets.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.990
<i>I wish I could've had some...</i>

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.640
Will you be stuck at work for a while?

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.240
<i>Yeah, we're just getting to the 
important part of the dig.</i>

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:21.010
<b>Fujitaka:        Dig starts today. Leaving in the afternoon. 
I made bread. It's in the fridge. 

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.430
<i>They say it's going to rain all next week,</i>

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:21.000
<i>so we want to get as much done as we can.</i>

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.350
I know your research is important, 
but don't push yourself too hard, okay?

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.280
<i>Thanks. I'll be careful.</i>

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.910
<i>Anything different going on there?</i>

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:33.020
Oh, I changed out Mom's photo!

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.640
I found a really nice one in an album.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.390
<i>I wish I could've seen that...</i>

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:41.260
I'll leave it out. You can see it 
when you come home.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.850
<i>Yeah. I'll do my best.</i>

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.390
<i>Tell Toya-kun I called, okay?</i>

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:47.500
I will!

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.790
I'm worried about Dad. 
He's been so busy, lately.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:59.250
I'll try harder to have something good for him 
to eat when he gets home, every day, Mom.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.580
I've had so many phone calls, today.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.100
<b>Akiho-chan</b>

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.100
<b>Kinomoto</b>

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:10.950
Hello.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.110
Hello! Welcome, Akiho-chan!

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:17.610
Are you sure it's all right for 
me to come over this late?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.490
Of course!

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:23.200
My dad's at work, and my
brother's busy at college.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.760
Come on in!

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:25.740
Okay.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.850
Thank you for having me!

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.140
Something smells good...

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.370
I did my best, since you said 
you were coming over.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.000
You'll eat while you're here, right?

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:39.720
Are you sure?

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.050
I was a little lonely on my own, 
so I'm glad you're here!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.000
Does Kaito-san know?

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.440
Yes, I told him.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.040
Oh...

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.210
Here. Kaito-san sent these.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.340
He said we should eat them together.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:56.760
Can I open it?

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.740
They're so cute!

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.370
They taste great, too!

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.720
I-I'm sorry for being so loud...

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.400
I can't wait. Let's eat them in my room.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.160
I made iced tea.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:21.580
Okay.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:30.630
Pretty cramped, isn't it?

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.170
It's a very, <i>very</i> cute room!

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:39.020
Thanks. My brother's always yelling 
at me to clean it up, though.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.530
It looks very clean!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.030
I bet your room is beautiful, Akiho-chan.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.730
It isn't, really.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:49.400
It's just full of books.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.530
Can I see your room, the next 
time I visit your house?

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.240
Of course!

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:59.870
I haven't invited anyone over since 
moving into my current house.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.430
Really?

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:08.800
My family only invites people 
we're very close to.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:16.460
Does that mean Tomoyo-chan 
and I are very close to you?

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:19.750
Yes!

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.580
I diluted the tea with a little soda.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.170
Are carbonated drinks okay?

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:25.770
Yes.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:31.030
I'm so glad I met you and Tomoyo-san 
when I moved to Japan.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.320
<i>It's nice that they're good friends now.</i>

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.200
<i>Still, I hid here in a hurry,</i>

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.100
<i>but it sure is cramped...</i>

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.640
These are so good!

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.890
I guess we shouldn't eat too 
many before dinner, huh?

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:43.340
Kaito-san said they'll keep for a while.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.300
Please share them with your family.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:49.310
Sure! I'll just have one mor—

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.540
Is something wrong?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.180
<b>You're eatin' that? You're really eatin' that?</b>

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.560
No, nothing!

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.010
Kaito-san sure is a great cook, isn't he?

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.730
He can do everything!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:07.200
I've been wanting to do whatever I can for 
myself, to make it easier for him, but...

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.990
I'm sure you're good at lots of things.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.980
I'm <i>extremely</i> clumsy!

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:16.390
I'm especially bad at cooking and sewing...

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:19.800
You should have Tomoyo-chan 
teach you how to sew!

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:24.790
She made this. And this, and this.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.170
She made all of these costumes for me!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:34.230
She does both the designs and 
the stitching all by herself.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.420
That's amazing!

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:39.760
She surprises me every time. 
They're really comfortable, too.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:40.930
They're wonderful!

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.800
When did you wear them?

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:46.330
U-Uh, well...

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:51.130
<i>The costumes Tomoyo made for Sakura 
obviously ain't normal street clothes.</i>

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:53.310
<i>It'd even be a stretch to wear 
'em on special occasions!</i>

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:56.500
W-Well, I was in this play... 
And I wore them for that!

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.960
Nice cover-up!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.620
<b>Good job!</b>

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.860
I wish I could have seen it.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.350
Oh! Do you have any photos or anything?

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.490
N-Not of these outfits...

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.620
But I have some of another costume.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.020
You were a princess?

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.140
Y-Yeah.

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:16.760
It looks like all the others were in it, too.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.390
But where's Tomoyo-san?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:21.900
She sang instead, so she wasn't in the play.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.890
Tomoyo-san is certainly a wonderful singer.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:26.080
Yeah!

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:27.860
Who is this?

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:29.990
That's Meiling-chan.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:33.190
She's Syaoran-kun's cousin. 
She's in Hong Kong, right now.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:34.940
She's very pretty.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:37.990
Yeah! I was just on the phone 
with her earlier, today.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:37.990
<b>Nadeshiko Festival</b>

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:41.630
Is Li-kun playing a prince here?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:42.500
Yeah.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.080
You both look lovely!

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:48.010
Did anyone record a video of it?

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.890
A-Actually, yes.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:51.730
Please let me watch it!

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.900
S-Sure... I-Is next time okay?

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.880
Of course! I look forward to it!

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.560
So this is what Japanese schools are like...

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.390
Akiho-chan, have you ever 
worn things like dresses?

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:09.520
Sometimes, at parties and such.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.900
I'd love to see a picture of you 
wearing one, sometime.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.670
O-Of me?

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.770
Yeah! I'm sure it'd be beautiful!

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:20.020
I might not go so far as to say that...

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:22.810
But I'll show you.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.600
We should have dinner now.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.780
Could you help me set the table?

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:30.290
Sure!

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:32.990
Should I carry this, then?

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:36.300
Thanks! Sorry to make you help, 
when you're my guest.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.300
Don't... Don't forget to save some for me!

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.850
You can leave the door open.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:39.640
Okay.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.600
Should I put it here?

00:09:58.600 --> 00:09:59.350
Yeah.

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.580
Akiho-chan, can you eat onions?

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.190
I like onions.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.570
Is there anything you don't like?

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.790
Not especially... Oh.

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:11.370
I don't like konjac, actually...

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.220
Really?

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.550
It's not the konjac's fault at all,

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:17.340
but that texture...

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.220
I'm the same!

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:22.220
<b>Jiggle</b>

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.150
I can't stand konjac!

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.560
You, too?

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.730
Don't worry! Even if we don't like konjac,

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:28.880
the people we love will eat it for us!

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:31.550
Like, at my house, there's my brother.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:34.790
Now that you mention it, 
Kaito-san likes konjac, too.

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:37.140
Yeah! So konjac is...

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.230
Yes! It's no problem!

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:41.770
I'm so glad for the konjac.

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:42.540
Me, too.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.030
<i>Is that really the issue here?!</i>

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.650
I hope it all turned out okay...

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:00.340
Oh, but I know the bread will be good!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.240
My dad made it and kept it in the fridge.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.750
It looks delicious!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.250
Let's eat.

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:09.270
Dinnertime!

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.390
Wh-What do you think?

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.910
It's really delicious!

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.670
I'm so glad...

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:34.160
I've made it lots of times, 
and I did taste it,

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.990
but I was still a little nervous.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.260
It's very mild.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:42.500
But it's a bit different from 
other beef stews I've eaten.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:48.060
There's a little bit of miso in it.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.350
So it has a secret ingredient!

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.340
It's nothing that special, but I guess so.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:55.740
My brother taught me that trick.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:00.270
Then, everyone in your family can cook?

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:01.930
Yeah. We take turns.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:08.700
<b>Cleaning | Cooking | Laundry |
Mon. | Sakura | Toya | Fujitaka | 
Tue. | Fujitaka | Sakura | / | 
Wed. | Toya | Fujitaka | Sakura |
Thu. | / | Toya | / |
Fri. | Toya | Sakura | Toya |
Sat. | Toya | Fujitaka | / |
Sun. | Sakura | Sakura | Sakura |</b>

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:06.300
When I was little, I wasn't 
allowed to fry anything.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.700
But once I started middle 
school, it was okay.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.950
So you made this, too?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.710
Yeah... Though I'm still practicing those.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.060
It's delicious!

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.220
I'll have another one.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:27.540
Do the others in your family cook?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.570
Everyone in my family is too busy,

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:34.110
so the people who work for 
us take care of everything.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.160
Like Kaito-san?

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.160
Yes.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.860
That's pretty amazing!

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.110
It's not amazing at all.

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:46.860
All of you are far more amazing because 
you can do things for yourselves.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:48.910
No, not at all...

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:52.370
People still do things for me 
and help me all the time.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:56.730
Would you teach me how to cook, Sakura-san?

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:57.630
Huh?

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.130
B-But I'm not that good,

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:04.530
and I'm sure Kaito-san would 
be a much better teacher!

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:08.400
I want to improve at it without 
letting Kaito-san know.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:18.070
I guess you want Kaito-san 
to eat your cooking, huh?

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.140
I know that feeling.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.970
You want the person you like

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.050
to eat good food.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:36.170
Yes.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.990
Then, let's get better together!

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:39.820
Together?

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:42.040
Yeah!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.040
I'm still practicing myself,

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.330
so I'll work hard with you!

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.100
Okay!

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.080
Do you want more beef stew?

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.820
Yes, please.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.590
That reminds me!

00:13:56.590 --> 00:13:59.510
I just borrowed a book on cat's 
cradle from the library.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:01.150
Let's try it together after dinner.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.470
I'd love to!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.690
I'm back!

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:17.860
Is this enough beef stew?

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.700
Let me know if it's too much.

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.580
Akiho-chan?

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:28.310
Did you have trouble sleeping last night?

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:33.000
I'm sorry. I didn't, really, but...

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.010
Don't force yourself. 
Do you need to lie down?

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:38.530
No.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.130
I'm all right...

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:47.790
Akiho-chan?!

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:58.030
What happened, Saku—

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:01.450
What happened, Sakura?

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:04.340
Akiho-chan suddenly fell asleep!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.490
What?

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:08.790
Akiho-chan... Akiho-chan!

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.310
Was she sick or somethin'?

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:15.320
She didn't seem sick.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:17.010
Something just...

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:20.760
That!

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:21.890
What?

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:27.770
Did that floaty thing put her to sleep?

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.080
I think so.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:32.750
She's not hurt.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:35.350
She really is just sleeping.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:36.590
Yeah.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.480
If I don't take care of that thing,

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:43.160
will Akiho-chan sleep forever?

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.480
If this is a card's work, then probably so.

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:52.370
Just hang on, Akiho-chan.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:56.600
Let's go.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:57.460
Right.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.450
Flank it!

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:05.030
Kero-chan!

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.430
Forget about me... After that thing...

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:07.890
Right!

00:16:07.890 --> 00:16:09.280
Man, that hurt!

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.370
Wait!

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.890
Sakura!

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.640
Well? Did ya capture it?

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:23.650
What the heck is this?!

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.580
What's goin' on here?

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.060
What is this?

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:35.260
Another dimension is right outside the house!

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.110
Kero-chan, did you sense anything?

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:40.290
Nah, still nothing.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:46.110
I'm going to capture that thing!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:49.700
Let's go.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:50.730
All right!

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:02.000
Wow, we haven't done somethin' 
like this in a long time...

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:06.600
Quit... Quit dartin' around!

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.780
Hold it right there, darn it! Grr!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.810
<i>Release!</i>

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.280
<i>Gravitation!</i>

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.730
<i>Gravitation!</i>

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.380
What now? I can't capture it.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.310
How about usin' Siege to encircle it?

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:49.710
I'll try it.

00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:51.990
<i>Siege!</i>

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.120
How'd that happen?

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:15.140
I get it. This space we're 
in now is a card, too.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:17.610
So you can't encircle it with Siege?

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:21.020
What should we do? Try to flank it again?

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:23.020
That thing's surprisingly quick.

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.380
You think it'll walk up while 
we're waitin' in ambush?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.070
Ambush?

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.310
If we make sure it doesn't notice us...

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:34.910
Kero-chan, go on ahead!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:35.900
All right!

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:39.180
My turn to take you on!

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.910
Oh... Now, I get it!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.950
Now, Sakura!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.650
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:08.850
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.100
<i>Secure!</i>

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:26.800
"Snooze"...

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:30.590
So this is what made Akiho-chan fall asleep.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.600
<b>Snooze</b>

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:32.580
Sakura...

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.270
Sorry.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.110
I was about to enter eternal sleep myself...

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:43.070
Sakura! We gotta hurry!

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:44.030
Yeah!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.850
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:48.940
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:50.160
<i>Secure!</i>

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:11.450
"Labyrinth."

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:14.650
<b>Labyrinth</b>

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.360
Labyrinth...

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.360
I get it.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:20.890
Even if you encircle a labyrinth, 
you still can't get out of it.

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:27.330
This is where we were?!

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.640
We have to get home before 
Akiho-chan wakes up!

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.360
Careful!

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:39.000
I can't believe I fell asleep 
while visiting your house!

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:41.120
Don't worry about it!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.510
<b>Nervous</b>

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.520
Yeah, it was the card's fault.

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.340
You can just come over again, then.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:50.610
Huh?

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:53.670
We have a library downstairs.

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:56.530
I'll ask my dad if we can go in.

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.480
So come over again, okay?

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:01.730
Sakura-san...

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.840
Just a sec.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:08.730
Yes? Who is it?

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.480
<i>Forgive my intrusion.</i>

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:13.760
I'm sorry you had to come get me.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:15.760
Think nothing of it.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:19.570
Kinomoto-sama, thank you 
for all you've done today.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:21.630
You don't need to use "sama" for me.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:22.820
But...

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.030
Just "Sakura" is fine.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:30.650
Then, may I call you "Sakura-san"?

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:32.150
Y-Yes!

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:35.460
Thank you so much for having me today.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.390
Thank you for coming. I had fun.

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:40.050
Thank you very much!

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:46.480
Oh, forgive me. I couldn't help myself.

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.610
Please don't mind me.

00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:05.720
Sakura-san is a wonderful person, isn't she?

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:07.590
She really is.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:12.720
She's pretty and kind. And she always 
shows her concern for others.

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:14.960
For you, as well?

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:16.350
Yes.

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:21.320
I'm glad to hear that.

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:31.220
I hope I can become even better 
friends with Akiho-chan.

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:12.350
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:16.500
It's your ultimate reward for workin' 
so hard: "Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.640
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.640
<b>K</b>

00:24:16.500 --> 00:24:19.640
Today, you get to hear one of my special 
talks, for as long as time allows!

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:19.640
<b>We'll stop the camera!</b>

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:23.140
It's the battle costume Tomoyo 
made for that kid...

00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:25.100
Tomoyo added her own sense to

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.040
the ceremonial outfit he 
wore in elementary school.

00:24:27.040 --> 00:24:29.200
Its highly precise measurements 
fit perfectly,

00:24:29.200 --> 00:24:30.700
so it's super easy to move in.

00:24:30.700 --> 00:24:32.490
Man, I'm so jealous.

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:32.490
<b>Watch how you talk!</b>

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:36.720
I guess that kid picked up the pretentious 
ability to pull a sword from his hand, huh?

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:37.240
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:37.240
<b>K</b>

00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:38.370
That'd be a hit at a year-end party.

00:24:38.370 --> 00:24:39.750
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:43.000
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.550 --> 00:24:44.120
I've come to Penguin Park after 
sensing a new card, and it's awful!

00:24:44.120 --> 00:24:45.880
The playground equipment is upside-down.

00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:48.980
I have to do something before 
it makes the news again!

00:24:48.380 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura and the Upside-down Penguin</b>

00:24:48.980 --> 00:24:51.640
Next time, "Sakura and the 
Upside-down Penguin."

00:24:51.640 --> 00:24:54.710
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:24:56.350
<b>End</b>
